# This project deploys shell scripts and configs to Linux.
# A CRLF line ending in a .sh file causes: bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M
# It has already bitten this project twice (a \r in a .env secret silently broke
# webhook HMAC; an sshd drop-in that never applied). Force LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.ini  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# The NAP schema is the authoritative artefact and is WINDOWS-1251.
# Never let line-ending normalisation touch it - keep the bytes exactly as published.
nap/spec/** -text -diff
nap/*.zip binary
